LICENSING — THIS REPOSITORY IS SPLIT
------------------------------------

Upstream Mattermost is licensed in two parts. From the root LICENSE.txt of the
pinned tree:

    You are licensed to use the source code in Admin Tools and Configuration
    Files (server/templates/, server/i18n/, server/public/, webapp/ and all
    subdirectories thereof) under the Apache License v2.0.

The remainder of the platform is under the GNU Affero General Public License
v3.0, or a commercial license from Mattermost, Inc.

This repository mirrors that split rather than collapsing it, so that the wire
types stay reusable under the more permissive terms:

    crates/mm-model/          Apache-2.0     derived from server/public/model/
                                             full text: crates/mm-model/LICENSE

    crates/mm-store/          AGPL-3.0-only  derived (as they gain content) from
    crates/mm-app/                           server/channels/store/, /app/ and
    crates/mm-api/                           /api4/, which are AGPL v3.0
    crates/mm-ws/                            full text: ./LICENSE

    everything else           AGPL-3.0-only  the repository default

Apache-2.0 is one-way compatible with AGPL-3.0, so the AGPL crates may depend on
mm-model. The reverse is not true: mm-model must never take code, or a
dependency, from an AGPL-licensed crate or from server/channels/. That
constraint is the same one the existing dependency rule already enforces —
mm-model has zero internal dependencies — but it is now a licensing requirement
and not only an architectural one.

The four AGPL crates are still stubs at the time of writing. They carry
AGPL-3.0-only ahead of holding any AGPL-derived line, deliberately: the label is
a precondition for the first such commit, not a consequence of it.


MODIFICATIONS
-------------

Apache License 2.0, section 4(b) requires derivative works to carry prominent
notices stating that files have been changed. They have been, extensively, and
the same is true of the AGPL-licensed portion:

This project is a **translation** of Mattermost server source from Go to Rust.
No file here is a copy of an upstream file. Every Rust module is a
reimplementation of the corresponding Go source, restructured for Rust's type
system, and in a small number of documented cases it deliberately behaves
differently from the original. Those divergences are enumerated in
`docs/TECH_DEBT.md`; the per-file semantics are recorded in `MIGRATION.md`.

Rust source files cite their Go origin in a doc comment, for example:

    //! Port of `server/public/model/channel.go`.

Files under `fixtures/` are generated by running the upstream Go code and
recording its output; they contain no upstream source.


